<title>USA: Sinclair amended 10-Q raises net income.</title>
<headline>Sinclair amended 10-Q raises net income.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.06		    $0.10</p>
<p> Net		 1,969		    3,050</p>
<p> Revs		79,141		   54,179</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  34,750		   30,150</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.04		    $0.02</p>
<p> Net		 1,511		    507</p>
<p> Revs		126,910		  96,874</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  34,750		   29,575</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Full company name is Sinclair Broadcast Group</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said it was amending its 10-Q due to purchase accounting adjustments for the River City acquisition and that this did not affect total revenues or broadcast cash flow. The amendment resulted in a net income rise from a loss of $332,000 to income of $2 million for the three months ended June 30, 1996 and a rise in net income from a loss of $790,000 to income of $1.5 million for the first six months 1996.</p>
</text>
